    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d460">

                <pb facs="0473" n="465" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg465"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.00/1789: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-09-30T11:00:00+03:25">September 30, 1941—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 1—8:57 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>173. The British Minister informs me that Eden has informed Maisky<anchor n="52"
                        xml:id="d460-f1"/> that he considers any undue interference in Iranian
                    affairs or sympathy towards separatist movements by Russian forces in north of
                    Iran would be most harmful. The Ambassador promised to communicate this
                    information to his Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d460-f1" n="52" xml:id="d460-f1-content">
                <p>Ivan Maisky, Soviet Ambassador in the United Kingdom.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
